drivers/gpu/drm/virtio from CentOS Stream 10's kernel at tag
kernel-6.12.0-211.el10 (commit 7de4a4e89f63b47286cefbfbfe085c155d30d2fe,
gitlab.com/redhat/centos-stream/src/kernel/centos-stream-10, fetched file by
file), the tree RHEL 10.2 and AlmaLinux 10.2 build their 6.12.0-211.*.el10_2
kernels from. The kernel number stays 6.12 but Red Hat backports DRM: this
driver is upstream's of about v6.18 (drm_client_setup, aperture helpers,
drm_format_info in framebuffer init, the panic helpers, virtio_gpu_shutdown;
no DRM vblank), not 6.12's, and the headers have hrtimer_setup and no
hrtimer_init. Built and checked against the 6.12.0-211.7.3.el10_2 and
6.12.0-211.64.1.el10_2 kernel-devel headers. CentOS Stream 10 from
kernel-6.12.0-262.el10 on carries a driver identical to ../virtio-7.0 and
uses that variant (see ../virtio-7.0/ORIGIN). The AnyOS patch in ../patches-el10 applies on top of
exactly this copy. GPL-2.0 (the kernel's licence), see each file's SPDX line.
